A clean install knows it is clean
=================================

Everything here is about the first ten minutes: what a new person is asked, in what order, and
what the app decides on their behalf before they have decided anything.

**Nothing is pre-selected.** The choice object was born holding `ollama-cloud`, the setup table
selected it explicitly on load, and the status line fell back to the first catalog entry when the
dropdown was untouched — so a clean install displayed "Ollama Cloud" and read as already
configured. All three are gone. The provider select opens on `Choose a provider…`, there is no
status line until something is chosen, and Connect refuses with "Choose a provider first."

**The provider and key fields really are hidden now.** They were created with `hidden` and shown
anyway, because `.first-run-cloud { display: flex }` in the stylesheet beats the attribute — which
is only a suggestion from the browser's own sheet. An explicit `[hidden] { display: none
!important }` makes hidden mean hidden, so the two fields do not exist on screen until the card is
chosen.

**The section reads as a sequence.** "Choose a provider" heads it, with one paragraph of real
guidance — Ollama Cloud is the cheapest way in because it is a small monthly allowance rather than
per-token billing, which matters when a budget is fixed; a local model costs nothing after the
download; anything OpenAI-compatible works. The key page is a clickable `Get a key ↗` instead of a
URL printed inside a sentence.

**Nous Portal is a provider.** `https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1` answers with a normal
OpenAI model list, so it needed no special case: one base URL, one key, the models the portal
actually serves.

**The task list moved into the conversation.** It is no longer a page in the sidebar; it is a widget
under the composer, numbered from zero, with a status button that cycles, and it keeps its frame
when the list is empty so clearing the list does not clear the widget.

**The onboarding gate** now requires an explicit `completed: true` to be skipped, rather than
anything-but-false. Back navigation therefore lands on onboarding on an install with no history,
because the last history entry is the new-instance page and that page is now the gate. The back
arrow asks the gate rather than the history stack, so repeated backs cannot run out of entries and
strand somebody in an empty chat.

**Nothing offers a model before there is a provider.** The Choose model control — in the top bar
and in the composer — is absent until setup is answered. A picker that opens onto an empty catalog
is a dead end, and first run is exactly when somebody is most likely to press it.

**The task widget resizes.** Vertical only: how much of the list to keep in view is a judgement
about the work, and dragging its width would fight the composer underneath.

**A way back in.** "Onboarding (development)" sits above Settings, so seeing the wizard again does
not require deleting a profile.

